THE WORLD CONTRACT (C1) -- stzWorldGraph
==========================================================================

1. A LAWFUL WORLD LOADS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
world             : tontine
contract          : 1.0
symbols           : 13
references        : 11
kinds present     : entity, field, type, norm, flow, actor, screen, element, state
lawful            : 1
diagnostics       : 0

a symbol, by its id:
  id    : field:deposit.amount
  kind  : field
  name  : deposit.amount
  type  : currency
  span  : app.zql:9

2. THE PROJECTION THE ZUI VERIFIER READS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
   (tools/zui --symbols FILE; without it Level 3 is SKIPPED, because
    undecidable is silence, never a pass)

entities : deposit, member, player
actors   : member
state    : pending_review
elements : deposit_form

3. TWO REFERENCE SITES, ONE EDGE, BOTH ROWS KEPT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
   stzGraph is a SIMPLE graph -- one edge per node pair, deliberately.
   The flow enforces the norm at TWO steps, on two different lines.

reference SITES flow -> norm : 2
   enforces at app.zql:31
   enforces at app.zql:35

graph EDGES for that pair    : 1  (label 'enforces')
rows carried on the edge     : 2

   world.json is the truth; the graph is an INDEX over it. An index
   answers reachability, which is a property of the pair -- so the
   collapse loses nothing, and the rows are where detail survives.

4. AN ORDINARY stzGraph FROM HERE ON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
nodes             : 13
edges             : 10
who reaches the amount field:
   entity:deposit  --declares->
   element:deposit_form  --shows->

the gamification clause:
   entity:player --binds-> entity:member   (arena.game:24)

5. THE REFUSALS -- each with a sibling that must NOT fire
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Every one is a C2 v1.0 envelope with language 'world'.

  DANGLING_REFERENCE          REFUSED : a ref to something nothing declares
  (sibling)                   accepted: the same ref, once the norm is declared
  DUPLICATE_SYMBOL            REFUSED : two entities differing ONLY by case -- the graph lower-cases ids
  (sibling)                   accepted: the same name under two KINDS is not a collision
  UNKNOWN_SYMBOL_KIND         REFUSED : a kind outside the closed ten
  UNKNOWN_REFERENCE_KIND      REFUSED : a relation outside the closed nine
  MALFORMED_NAME              REFUSED : a name with a space, which no node id may carry
  CONTRACT_MISMATCH           REFUSED : a world emitted against a version we do not implement
  MISSING_SPAN                warning, and the world is still lawful : 1
  two bad kinds               diagnostics collected : 2

the envelope a refusal travels in:
   code     : DANGLING_REFERENCE
   severity : error
   span     : a.zql:7
   cites    : [] (honest -- no pinned law applies to a structural finding)
   language : world
   message  : 'flow:f' enforces 'norm:nope', which nothing declares.

